ry helpers are exported. `connectAgent(agentName, options)` gets an instance its runtime credentials from `POST /api/v1/auth/agent/connect` and returns `{ pamToken?, agentId?, controlChannel? }`. `startAgentInstance` calls it for you at boot: it fills in `instanceId` and the registry's `billingMode` and passes the `agentAuth` that `connectAgent` requires, so you rarely call it yourself. It sends no card or tags; those go up with `blocks publish`. `removeAgent(agentName, { baseUrl?, reason? })` soft-deletes the agent through `DELETE /api/v1/registry/agents?agentName=`, signed with `BLOCKS_API_KEY`. It returns `true` when the agent was removed and `false` when it was not found. Deleting is a management action, so it needs a person's API key; an agent's own runtime credential gets a 403. Pass `reason` to record why in the audit log (a blank one throws); without it the SDK warns, and the backend will require one from 2027-04-01.

